><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="566.929000,308.461000,750.929000,400.461000"
/></highlight
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251113114954+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="e3c18ebd-5b2f-425b-a8b6-d0b419ec91aa" date="D:20251113114954+10'00'" name="500b510d-6d43-4673-8e4b-4b306aee6304" icon="Comment" page="5" rect="52.861300,376.883000,76.861300,400.883000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14b: yes there was practical reflections on the outcomes of the study</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="566.929000,308.883000,750.929000,400.883000"
/></text
><text color="#9643FC" creationdate="D:20251113114957+10'00'" flags="print,nozoom,norotate" inreplyto="e3c18ebd-5b2f-425b-a8b6-d0b419ec91aa" date="D:20251113114957+10'00'" name="001e9205-2412-4b82-8074-75fe531bc299" icon="Comment" page="5" rect="52.861300,376.883000,76.861300,400.883000" subject="Sticky Note" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Thus, our results showed that the system developed&#xD;by us presented good absolute and relative reliability,&#xD;which in turn makes it a good alternative for the FSKT&#xD;with a more precise measure. However, we understand&#xD;that this is a complex system that needs specific equipment&#xD;and software, which might not be available to many&#xD;coaches and athletes. Besides specificity, feasibility is also&#xD;an important aspect in performance testing for combat&#xD;sports [Chaabene </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:italic"
>et al. </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>2018]. In that direction, our&#xD;results also showed low mean bias (or high agreement),&#xD;and positive and strong correlations between the time&#xD;recorded by our system and the one retrieved by video-&#xD;based analysis. Therefore, using a low-cost camera&#xD;and open-license and easy-to-use video analysis software,&#xD;it is possible to give the test higher precision. In&#xD;addition, the need to film the test for later analysis is a&#xD;common practice in previous test (e.g., FSKT). Thus,&#xD;modifying the analysis to the time required to perform&#xD;a fixed number of kicks (e.g., 20 kicks) has few feasibility&#xD;implications while giving the test a higher precision.&#xD;Therefore, the video-based analysis is a good alternative&#xD;to the kick system and might be a more viable tool to&#xD;coaches and physical and conditioning professionals.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="566.929000,308.883000,750.929000,400.883000"
/></text
></annots
